From b390fc7ed6ce57e3ced324cfda87c88df14b235b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jcs130 <lzl1992@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:22:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tts): preserve slow local speech ownership across reply
 turns
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

回归报告 / Regression Report

Slow local VoxCPM2 audio was emitted without its source speech ID, so the
host could assign an older sentence to a newer reply. Keep source identity
through worker output, audio headers, replay acknowledgement and frontend
completion after a text turn advances. A duplicate terminal notice must not
finish the next turn. Preserve cancellation epochs and legitimate repeated
sentences instead of muting by text.

Extend the existing bounded local playback watchdog from the last actual
audio delivery while long speech continues. Other providers keep the old
timeout. Add hashes/counts and playback boundary metadata without saving
speech text, PCM, prompts or credentials.

Validation: source-owner, fallback-ledger, frontend late-completion and
long-playback regressions failed before their fixes. Related regression:
2126 passed, one unchanged logger-capture test deselected after reproducing
its failure on the original 02c325c revision. Ruff, Node syntax and diff
checks passed. Risks covered include interrupts, provider fallback, audio
framing, late chunks and legitimate repeated replies. Native listening
acceptance is recorded separately; unit success is not audible acceptance.
